<prov:Activity rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#GenerationActivity">
  <rdfs:label>Ontology generation by OntoGeneration Agent (step 12)</rdfs:label>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#RefinedTerms"/>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#ProposedAxioms"/>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#ProposedTests"/>
  <prov:generated rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo#"/>
  <prov:wasInformedBy rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#TestGenerationActivity"/>
  <prov:wasAssociatedWith rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
  <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
  <prov:hadPlan rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#GenerationPrompt"/>
  <prov:qualifiedAssociation>
    <prov:Association>
      <prov:agent rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
      <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/awo_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
    </prov:Association>
  </prov:qualifiedAssociation>
  <vaem:rationale>The ontology models the supplied classes (Animal, Herbivore, PlantPart, Plant, Diet), object properties (eats, diet), and named individuals (Lion, CarnivorousDiet, PlantBasedDiet) to answer all atomic competency questions. Domain/range axioms for eats are multi-valued per CQ1/CQ3/CQ4/CQ6/CQ7, so they are explicitly listed in the Axioms field alongside the primary Domain/Range declarations. Herbivore is subclassed under Animal per CQ2. Individuals are typed to their respective classes. All proposed axioms and Themis tests are materialized.</vaem:rationale>
</prov:Activity>

